{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For his compassion was stirred.</b> After the manner of brothers from the same father and mother. <b>And in the Midrash:</b> כי נכמרו רחמיו אל אחיו — 'his compassion was stirred toward his brother.' He was asked: Do you have a brother from your mother? He said to him: I had a brother and I do not know where he is. Do you have children? He said to him: I have ten sons. He said to him: And what are their names? בלע ובכר ואשבל, etc. He said to him: And what is the significance of these names? He said to him: After the name of my brother and the troubles that overtook him: בלע — because he was swallowed up (נבלע) among the nations; בכר — because he was the firstborn (בכור) of his mother; אשבל — because he was taken captive (נשבה) among the nations; גרא — because he sojourned (גר) in a foreign land among the nations; נעמן — because his deeds were pleasant (נעימים); אחי — that he was my brother from the same father and mother; ראש — because he was older than I and a crown (עטרה) for my head; מפים — because he learned Torah from the mouth (מפי) of my father, all that he learned was from there; ועבר — and passed; וחפים — because he has been hidden (נתחפה) until this day. Another interpretation: מפים וחפים — he did not act deceptively in my regard and I did not act deceptively in his regard; וארד — after the name that our father said (Genesis 37:35): ״כי ארד אל בני אבל שאולה.״ And some say that his face was like a rose (ורד). Immediately: ויבקש לבכות ויבא החדרה ויבך שמה — 'And he sought to weep, and he entered the chamber and wept there.' And so it is also expounded in tractate Sotah."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:06.976670490Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}